---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_TAGLINE, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config/site.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description={`About ${SITE_NAME} — the free ${SITE_TAGLINE} that measures sound in your browser, keeps audio on your device, and stays ad-free for everyone.`}
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">About</p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-dark-ink"
    >
      About Us
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} started with a simple frustration: everyone occasionally
        needs to know how loud something is — a classroom, an open-plan office,
        a baby’s room, a workshop, a gig — and the answer was either a paid app
        full of ads or a hardware meter that costs more than it should. We
        thought the browser could do better.
      </p>

      <h2>What we build</h2>
      <p>
        We build small, focused tools that work the moment you open them. The
        {SITE_TAGLINE} is our flagship: a live gauge, a rolling 60-second
        graph, calibration against a reference meter, and a threshold alarm —
        all rendered locally, all free, with no account, no install, and no
        upsell. Every screen follows the same rule: the thing you came to do is
        the first thing you can do.
      </p>

      <h2>Why privacy is the product</h2>
      <p>
        A microphone tool only earns trust by never misusing the microphone.
        The audio stream is analysed in your browser with the Web Audio API and
        discarded sample by sample — nothing is recorded, buffered to disk, or
        transmitted. The only things we store are the preferences you choose
        (theme, calibration, alarm limit), and those live in your own browser’s
        storage, not on a server. You can read the full detail in our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How we keep it free</h2>
      <p>
        There is no advertising network on this site and we do not sell data —
        there is none to sell. The project is funded by the people who rely on
        it: schools, safety officers, musicians, and tinkerers who chip in when
        a tool saves them time. If {SITE_NAME} helped you, the best support is
        telling a colleague about it.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy, honestly stated</h2>
      <p>
        We take measurement seriously, which means being honest about limits.
        Device microphones differ, consumer hardware is not calibrated like a
        Class 2 sound level meter, and a browser cannot apply certified
        weighting filters. Our calibration offset closes most of the gap for
        everyday comparisons, but for regulatory or legal noise assessments
        you should always use a certified instrument. The tool is designed for
        awareness, education, and relative comparison — and it is very good at
        those.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, bug reports, or a feature idea? Write to us at
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or use the
        <a href="/contact-us/">contact page</a>. We read everything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
